39:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"compression"}]," has no storage of its own. It compresses on write, decompresses\non read, and hands the bytes to whatever is in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"backend"}],". The client sees raw\nbytes either way. Build artifacts are usually highly compressible, so this\nsaves disk in exchange for CPU; the only algorithm offered is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"lz4"}],", which is\nfast and gives up early on data that won't compress."]}]
3a:["$","p",null,{"children":["Because the wrapped store is a full spec rather than a reference to a type,\nwrappers nest arbitrarily. A ",["$","code",null,{"children":"verify"}]," around a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"size_partitioning"}]," whose upper\nhalf is a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"dedup"}]," whose index is a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," of memory-over-disk is not an\nexotic config; it's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config/examples/filesystem_cas.json5"}],", and\neach layer is doing one comprehensible job."]}]
